<title>GERMANY: GERMAN DATA DUE NEXT WEEK- FINAL CPI, RETAIL SALES.</title>
<headline>GERMAN DATA DUE NEXT WEEK- FINAL CPI, RETAIL SALES.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following German economic indicators are expected to be released next week:</p>
<p>    INDICATOR	PERIOD	 PREVIOUS		 EXPECTED</p>
<p>					    DATA		     DATE</p>
<p> Final CPI	   July	   +0.5 m/m, +1.8 y/y   Aug 12-13</p>
<p> Retail sales	June	   -2.3, -1.4	     Aug 12-13</p>
<p> Insolvencies	May	    -0.3 pct y/y	   Aug 12-13</p>
<p> Wholesale prices  July	   -0.3 m/m, +2.6 y/y   Aug 13-14</p>
<p>NOTE - The Federal Statistics Office said the expected release dates were targets. The previous CPI data show preliminary west German inflation for July. The retail sales data show the real and nominal year-on-year change, in percent.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
